# APU block-level variant of abc_balanced.script (same recipe minus one pass).
#
# Deviation from the whole-SoC recipe: the "&fraig -x" SAT-sweeping pass is
# removed. On the APU multiplier-dominated AIGs (apu_kernel_engine and the
# reconstruction/transform/resampler engines) "&fraig -x" does not terminate:
# measured 14+ hours at 100% CPU on the 163k-AND apu_kernel_engine network
# (yosys-abc 0.67, PDK_IHP130, 2026-09-16/17), with larger modules still
# pending behind it. With only that pass removed the same module maps in
# ~19 s and every other pass, the &nf delay target, and the tool versions are
# identical to the whole-SoC flow. The SoC recipe itself is untouched.

strash
&get -n
&put
scorr
dc2
dretime
strash
&get -n
&dch -f
&nf {D}
&put
buffer
upsize {D}
dnsize {D}
stime -p
